@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@ Auto-pilot pipeline:
 
 Authority generations and receipts remain bound to one originating PR head in the SHA-checked ledger. The runner first conditionally prepares that generation and writes its attempt-bound primary reservation. Finalization follows successful mark-running setup and remains a prerequisite for every worker job. Failure or cancellation before finalization conditionally releases only that non-authorizing preparation; cleanup is best effort and the workflow reporter must reconcile interrupted attempts. If that release response is lost, the same preflight-failed owner attempt may retry against the persisted released receipt, but a replacement preparation cannot be released by it. PR head and labels are separate GitHub state, so changed or unavailable evidence denies the result without refunding a consumed receipt. Confirmation uncertainty preserves the ledger and `needs-human`; automation never infers label ownership from a successful add or deletes a possibly concurrent human blocker. A confirmed receipt cannot be reopened merely because its hard label disappeared. The same worker attempt may retry confirmation once against its spent receipt, without granting a new execution. This is a fail-closed, at-most-one-grant protocol, not an atomic transaction across GitHub resources.
 
-The failed-run reporter reconciles the receipt even when the presentation summary never reached `running`, but only after the originating attempt's worker jobs positively show no worker step started. Worker job and step names come from keepalive-capable registry entries at the originating run's exact head (with naming-convention defaults); a newly registered provider does not require a reporter-side provider list, and a later registry change cannot turn a started old provider into false non-start evidence. Missing original registry evidence is unknown. Started or unknown worker evidence preserves the receipt. Presentation-summary inputs alone cannot prove non-start or refund a consumed receipt. An originating run concluded `skipped` has no failed attempt to reconcile and is ignored. Before preparing a receipt, the runner writes an immutable, exact-owner-attempt index on the authority branch; the PR ledger remains the grant authority. For sweep-triggered dispatches with no webhook PR association, the reporter directly reads that index and verifies its exact receipt against the PR ledger. A missing, conflicting or unreadable index fails explicitly for owner follow-up, never as proof of non-execution; associated runs avoid the index lookup. Consumer reporter deduplication includes the originating run ID and attempt so reruns remain independently recoverable. If the ordinary summary finishes first and rewrites `challenge-due` to `automation-retry`, it retains only the exact recovery owner attempt and prior generation when that attempt owns the current-head authority receipt (`authorityAttemptOwnsRecoveryReceipt`); unrelated non-authority runs that reconcile as `attempt-not-current` must not record `recovery_owner_attempt`. Projection accepts that cleared presentation state only when both markers match the reconciled receipt lineage; a generic blank generation never authorizes recovery. A running summary records its exact run attempt, and delayed projection requires that owner when the summary is running. Projection also re-reads the authoritative ledger immediately before publication and exits as superseded if another attempt has prepared, consumed, confirmed, replaced, or otherwise changed the settled receipt.
+The failed-run reporter reconciles the receipt even when the presentation summary never reached `running`, but only after the originating attempt's worker jobs positively show no worker step started. Worker job and step names come from keepalive-capable registry entries at the originating run's exact head (with naming-convention defaults); a newly registered provider does not require a reporter-side provider list, and a later registry change cannot turn a started old provider into false non-start evidence. Missing original registry evidence is unknown. Started or unknown worker evidence preserves the receipt. Presentation-summary inputs alone cannot prove non-start or refund a consumed receipt. An originating run concluded `skipped` has no failed attempt to reconcile and is ignored. Before preparing a receipt, the runner writes an immutable, exact-owner-attempt index on the authority branch; the PR ledger remains the grant authority. For sweep-triggered dispatches with no webhook PR association, the reporter directly reads that index and verifies its exact receipt against the PR ledger. A missing, conflicting or unreadable index fails explicitly for owner follow-up, never as proof of non-execution; associated runs avoid the index lookup. Consumer reporter deduplication includes the originating run ID and attempt so reruns remain independently recoverable. If the ordinary summary finishes first, an attempt that owns the current-head authority receipt (`authorityAttemptOwnsRecoveryReceipt`) retains `challenge-due`, the exact recovery owner attempt, and the prior generation; it must not dispatch an ordinary retry before reporter projection settles that receipt lineage. An unrelated non-authority run that reconciles as `attempt-not-current` must not record `recovery_owner_attempt`. Projection accepts recovery markers only when both match the reconciled receipt lineage; a generic blank generation never authorizes recovery. A running summary records its exact run attempt